# CORS Usage Discovery Rule

Detect the presence of CORS implementation to conditionally trigger comprehensive CORS assessment.

## Headers to Detect
Access-Control-Allow-Origin, Access-Control-Allow-Methods,
Access-Control-Allow-Headers, Access-Control-Allow-Credentials

## Framework Patterns

### JavaScript/Node.js
cors(), app.use(cors, require('cors'), import cors from, res.header('Access-Control

### Python
flask_cors, CORS(app), @cross_origin, django-cors-headers, CorsMiddleware

### Java/Spring
@CrossOrigin, CorsConfiguration, CorsRegistry, CorsFilter, allowedOrigins

### C#/.NET
UseCors, EnableCors, WithOrigins, AllowAnyOrigin, AllowCredentials

### PHP
header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin

### Ruby/Rails
rack-cors, origins '*'

### Go
cors.New, cors.Default, AllowedOrigins, rs/cors

### Configuration Files
YAML/JSON cors: enabled: true, XML <cors> or <cors-configuration>

## Conditional Rule Triggering

IF cors_usage_detected THEN
  APPLY 08-cors-severity-assessment.mdc

## Core Principle

Efficiently identify CORS implementation patterns to ensure comprehensive vulnerability assessment is applied when needed.
